---
import { render } from 'astro:content';
import CareerTrace from '../components/CareerTrace.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { buildInfo } from '../lib/build-info';
import { loadContent } from '../lib/content';
import { compareByStartDescending, formatPeriod } from '../lib/period';
import { createTechnologyNameLookup } from '../lib/technologies';

const { roles, education, technologies } = await loadContent();
const technologyName = createTechnologyNameLookup(technologies);
const rolesByRecency = [...roles].sort(compareByStartDescending);
const renderedRoles = await Promise.all(
  rolesByRecency.map(async (role) => ({ role, Content: (await render(role)).Content })),
);
const educationByRecency = [...education].sort(
  (first, second) => second.data.year - first.data.year,
);

const practices = [
  {
    claim: 'Slow or unreliable third-party calls do not run inside a request.',
    example:
      'At Eight Assets, bank-account creation moved from the sign-up request to a BullMQ worker with a persisted job row. Sign-up returned at once, and the provider’s bad days stopped being the user’s problem.',
    href: '/work/queued-bank-onboarding/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'I retry server faults and record client faults.',
    example:
      'The same worker throws only on a 5xx, so the queue retries server faults and never replays a 4xx that a retry cannot fix. Support re-queues by hand, and a job already marked processed is refused.',
    href: '/work/queued-bank-onboarding/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'Application code stays off the chain.',
    example:
      'At Gold Rush every operator-side contract call went through a backend that held the ABIs, addresses and operator key, so the pre-sale panel deployed with no secrets. At CI&T, the one key that could mint lived in a Lambda whose only job was to sign.',
    href: '/work/contract-backend-boundary/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'Reports read a read model, not the collection the workers write.',
    example:
      'On Integra.Sky, counts, indicators and billing read a slim execution-reference collection rather than the execution store every worker writes on every run.',
    href: '/work/ipaas-admin-indicators/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'I increment counters with an atomic update instead of read-modify-write.',
    example:
      'In the contest API, vote totals became an atomic update expression after the first version lost updates under concurrent voting.',
    href: '/work/design-contest-backend/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'Local development runs the real dependencies.',
    example:
      'The contest backend developed against local S3 and DynamoDB emulation. The mutual-TLS harness for the platform worker generates its own certificate authority in Docker Compose so the failure reproduces on a laptop.',
    href: '/work/mtls-poc/',
  },
  {
    claim: 'I reproduce a failure before fixing it.',
    example:
      'When a legacy consumer mis-handled accented characters, I wrote a mock endpoint that proved the charset behavior before touching the integration.',
    href: '/work/mock-endpoint/',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About · Rafael Thomazzi"
  description="How I work, stated as practices with the project that backs each one, the career trace, and education glossed for readers outside Brazil."
>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-fluid-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-6 text-fluid-lg">
      <p>
        I started in 2019 maintaining a school-management system in PHP, which taught me that most
        software work is reading someone else’s decisions. From 2020 I built features in a fintech
        platform’s API in Node.js and TypeScript: accounts, fees, cashback, identity checks, and the
        bank integrations behind them. In 2021 I wrote the layer between a token and NFT product and
        its contracts. Then I spent seven months at CI&T on blockchain-adjacent backends for two
        clients.
      </p>
      <p>
        From late 2022 to early 2026 I built and ran backend services of an integration platform at
        Sky.One, which is the work I had been circling the whole time: the code between systems,
        owned from design through the production issue. In 2026 I joined a payments group to work on
        a payment gateway. That role ended in 2026-09. I am from São Paulo state and I am looking
        for my next role, remote from Brazil.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="how-i-work" class="border-t border-rule py-12">
    <h2 id="how-i-work" class="font-mono text-xs tracking-label text-ink-muted uppercase">
      How I work
    </h2>
    <ol class="mt-6 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        practices.map(({ claim, example, href }) => (
          <li class="max-w-(--measure)">
            <p class="font-semibold">{claim}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">{example}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs">
              <a href={href}>
                Case study<span class="sr-only">: {claim}</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true"> →</span>
              </a>
            </p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="career" class="border-t border-rule py-12">
    <h2 id="career" class="font-mono text-xs tracking-label text-ink-muted uppercase">Career</h2>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <CareerTrace roles={roles} now={buildInfo.yearMonth} />
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-12">
      {
        renderedRoles.map(({ role, Content }) => (
          <article class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[16rem_minmax(0,var(--measure))]">
            <header class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{role.data.company}</h3>
              <p>{role.data.companyGloss}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-ink">{role.data.title}</p>
              <p>
                {formatPeriod(role.data.period)} · {role.data.location}
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2">{role.data.stack.map(technologyName).join(' · ')}</p>
            </header>
            <div class="prose">
              <Content />
            </div>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="education" class="border-t border-rule py-12">
    <h2 id="education" class="font-mono text-xs tracking-label text-ink-muted uppercase">
      Education
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 font-mono text-sm">
      {
        educationByRecency.map(({ data }) => (
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">
              {data.credential}, {data.field}
            </span>
            <span class="text-ink-muted">
              {' '}
              · {data.institution} · {data.year}
            </span>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted">
              {data.credentialGloss} · {data.institutionGloss}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
